         "text-align": "center"
        },
        "> .elementor-widget-container": {
         "padding": "1px 1px 1px 1px"
        }
       },
       "html": "<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Mark was born in Waterford Town, the home where the famous Waterford Crystal is made. </span><span style=\"color: var( --e-global-color-f3735e1 ); font-family: var( --e-global-typography-text-font-family ), Sans-serif; font-size: 1rem;\">He has been working with students the last 21 plus years in his job with education and his favorite pastime is the GAA. (Gaelic Athletic Association)  </span><span style=\"color: var( --e-global-color-f3735e1 ); font-family: var( --e-global-typography-text-font-family ), Sans-serif; font-size: 1rem;\">He loves all sports, but in particular his native sports of football and hurling.  </span><span style=\"color: var( --e-global-color-f3735e1 ); font-family: var( --e-global-typography-text-font-family ), Sans-serif; font-size: 1rem;\">Mark has been involved with the Irish Life Experience for over a decade coaching traditional Irish sports. He loves the program and loves how the students engage in all activities and their willingness to learn each and every year.  </span><span style=\"color: var( --e-global-color-f3735e1 ); font-family: var( --e-global-typography-text-font-family ), Sans-serif; font-size: 1rem;\">Mark is an avid music and film buff and also enjoys his down time with family and friends with cups of coffee and chats.</span></p>"
      }
     ],
     "width": 100
    }
